# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

A layered FastAPI service with liveness and readiness endpoints, JSON logs with request IDs, one
example resource kept in memory, and tests. It runs without any external service.

## Requirements

[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is the only tool you need. It installs Python {{ python_version }}+
and the development tools on demand.

## Run it

```bash
uv sync                                                # create .venv with the dev group
uv run uvicorn {{ package_name }}.main:app --reload    # http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs> for the interactive API documentation.

| Endpoint | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /health` | The process is up. Never touches dependencies. |
| `GET /ready` | Every readiness check passes; 503 otherwise. |
| `POST /api/v1/examples` | Create an example. |
| `GET /api/v1/examples` | List examples; `offset` and `limit` query parameters. |
| `GET /api/v1/examples/{example_id}` | Read one example. |
| `DELETE /api/v1/examples/{example_id}` | Delete one example. |

Examples live in process memory and are lost when the process stops.

## Configuration

Settings are in `{{ package_name }}/settings.py`. Override any of them with an environment variable
prefixed `{{ package_name | upper }}_`, or copy `.env.example` to `.env` for local values. `.env` is
git-ignored; never commit it. List values use JSON, for example
`{{ package_name | upper }}_ALLOWED_HOSTS='["api.example.com"]'`.

In production set `{{ package_name | upper }}_ENVIRONMENT=production` and a real
`{{ package_name | upper }}_ALLOWED_HOSTS`. Startup fails if `DEBUG` is on or `ALLOWED_HOSTS`
contains `*`. Requests with any other `Host` header get 400, so an orchestrator's probes must send
a host name that is in `ALLOWED_HOSTS`.

## Security

No secrets are needed to run this service. No authentication is included: add it before exposing
the service beyond a trusted network. The service does not check anything beyond the settings
described above.

## Checks

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Tests | `uv run pytest` |
| Lint | `uv run ruff check .` |
| Format check | `uv run ruff format --check .` |
| Type check | `uv run mypy {{ package_name }} tests` |

## Docker

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_name }} .
docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -e {{ package_name | upper }}_ALLOWED_HOSTS='["localhost"]' {{ project_name }}
```

The Dockerfile is not built or run by the generated checks; Docker is optional.

## Project layout

```
{{ package_name }}/
  main.py          # ASGI entry point
  app.py           # create_app(): settings, middleware, routers, repository
  settings.py      # typed settings and production checks
  logs.py          # JSON logging and request IDs
  domain/          # the example entity, its error, and the repository port
  application/     # use cases that depend only on the port
  infrastructure/  # in-memory repository
  api/             # routers, schemas, dependencies, error mapping
tests/             # settings, logs, use cases, HTTP behaviour
```

